Package: csemapp
Type: Package
Title: A Point-and-Click Interface for PLS-SEM with 'cSEM'
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person("Your", "Name", email = "wa274259@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Packages the 'cSEM GUI' Shiny application: an interactive drag-and-drop model
    builder (moderators and quadratic effects included), partial least squares (PLS) and
    consistent PLS estimation, parallel bootstrapping, importance-performance map analysis
    (IPMA), confirmatory tetrad analysis (CTA), cross-validated out-of-sample prediction
    (PLSpredict) with the cross-validated predictive ability test (CVPAT), a results diagram,
    and cSEM-style reports that can be copied to 'Word'/'Excel' or exported as 'Excel'
    workbooks. The application script is shipped unchanged in the package and started with
    run_csem_gui().
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    cSEM,
    jsonlite,
    shiny,
    utils,
    writexl
Suggests:
    knitr,
    parallel,
    rmarkdown,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
VignetteBuilder: knitr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/YOUR-USERNAME/csemapp
